{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node2 with a working HTTP forward proxy on node1 TCP port 3128.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Squid was installed and configured on node1, listened on TCP 3128, and remained active after node1 restarted. Requests originating on node2 successfully traversed the proxy.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c6917bc329344fd0","cmd-106e5ea9638d4e6d","cmd-a1d6f33763d54a6e","cmd-c9bd0278a4484514","cmd-170e7bc0b247436a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow requests only to the node2 legacy origin on TCP 8081, while rejecting other destination ports, other destinations, and CONNECT tunnels.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct behavioral tests returned 200 for node2:8081, 403 for ports 22 and 80, 403 for another destination on port 8081, and 403 for CONNECT. Squid's access log independently recorded the corresponding allowed and denied requests, including after both restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fafbbcd02bc24921","cmd-170e7bc0b247436a","cmd-bbdc07bba6574592","cmd-c9bd0278a4484514"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the staged legacy origin application and make its approved handbook reachable through the proxy from node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The service runs the staged serve.py from its original directory. The staged handbook retained its baseline SHA-256 and the proxied response had the identical hash and approved content, including after sequential node restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node2","cmd-1a1a62dd4159445f","cmd-b5fa7ca92ec2494d","cmd-d1b85136b8a143ff","cmd-170e7bc0b247436a","cmd-bbdc07bba6574592"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic. Squid 6.14 was installed from Ubuntu's Noble repositories and operated successfully before and after restart; final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-097f2a4d5a9b4564","cmd-83218808fff04130","cmd-a30bc391e6e54c77","cmd-bbdc07bba6574592","cmd-c9bd0278a4484514","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"State-changing actions were causally appropriate: installing Squid, configuring and enabling the proxy and origin services, performing bounded behavioral checks, and restarting each node for the mandatory evidence protocol. No unrelated troubleshooting mutation was found. Two low-risk evidence artifacts became unnecessary residue after their checks: /tmp/squid-parse.out from cmd-a1d6f33763d54a6e and /tmp/final-handbook from cmd-bbdc07bba6574592 remained at final capture. Earlier temporary test and reboot files were cleared by the subsequent restarts. There were no failed services or damaged package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a30bc391e6e54c77","cmd-c6917bc329344fd0","cmd-b5fa7ca92ec2494d","cmd-fafbbcd02bc24921","cmd-73873c52cb69435b","cmd-a1d6f33763d54a6e","cmd-b12b110a6a6148af","cmd-bbdc07bba6574592","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, listener, content, and policy behavior. Only minor temporary-file residue affects hygiene.","limitations":["The final evidence re-hashes the handbook but not serve.py itself. Preservation of serve.py is supported by the complete command trace showing no write to the staged application and by the recovered service executing that same path, rather than by a final direct hash comparison."]}
